  "basis": "The chart shows a positive correlation between advertising spend and sales across regions. Region E has the highest sales ($150K) and the highest spend ($70K), followed by Region D ($110K sales, $60K spend), and Region C ($80K sales, $50K spend). Regions A and B have lower spend and sales. The public task instructs to use the dashboard to choose a spend-increase decision. Given the clear trend of higher spend leading to higher sales, approving a broader region-wide spend increase aligns with the data, as it supports scaling successful strategies. The other options either delay action or limit scope, which contradicts the positive correlation shown.",
